# Payment Methods

Payment Methods are those elements where a scammer/organization will receive the funds from. This data is so important to take care and store, because it is the only way which a user
can search by to know if the person/company is talking to is legit or not. payment methods such as **card numbers**, **clabe** and **account numbers** are methods that can be hard to change for an individual (ask to the bank to change the number, go to the bank, etc), therefore, it is normal that a scammer/organization can change their usernames, emails, entities but can't change those numbers, which can be a great way to identify them easily. This last part is different when we are talking about **crypto wallets**, where they can change the public wallet identifier with no problem.

## Card numbers

Card numbers are composed with 16 numbers. We don't care if they're credit or debit. We should ignore the white spaces, usually they would be stripped out.

Example: 4152 3412 5132 1531 

## CLABE

CLABE (Clave Bancaria Estandarizada) is a identifier number that targets a bank account. This number is used by banks operating in **Mexico**. Usually, white spaces would be stripped out.

Example: 032 180 000118359719

## Account numbers

Account numbers are numbers used by the banks to identify their clients. They aren't shared between banks either public, usually the transfer of funds using this number works between accounts of the same bank.

Example: 010 3215312

## Crypto wallets

Crypto wallets are public hexadecimal addresses that represents a wallet of a blockchain (Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana,...).
These shouldn't have white spaces.

Example: 1A1zP1eP5QGefi2DMPTfTL5SLmv7DivfNa